<Field Guns Equipment>
</Field Guns Equipment>

<overview>
<p>The CCAF fields conventional infantry in larger numbers than its limited industrial base might suggest, drawing on the Confederation's deep tradition of citizens' militia service. Capellan soldiers learn to fight with fewer resources and less support than their counterparts in wealthier states, compensating with resourcefulness and ideological commitment. Mechanized tracked platoons give Capellan commanders infantry that can keep pace with armored formations across rough terrain. The tracked transports provide better cross-country mobility than wheeled vehicles, allowing these platoons to operate alongside the tanks and combat vehicles that form the CCAF's armored reserve. Light David gauss rifle sections carry precision electromagnetic weapons that deliver exceptional accuracy and penetration at range, making these platoons a serious threat to lightly armored targets.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on production date of David Light Gauss Rifle. Striker Carbine is standard CCAF long arm.
</notes>

